From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:20:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 317/333] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the Speak
 replies menu and cloud voices

One engine now speaks a whole response: its first spoken sentence locks the
voice, so the cloud list arriving or a menu pick mid-reply applies from the
next response and the device and cloud queues never overlap.

A stopped cloud playback's late completion no longer clears the next
playback's handlers. A failed voice list is retried instead of cached, with
one request in flight. A bare stored voice from before the prefixes counts as
no choice once the server has cloud voices; an explicit device choice wins.
The Voice hint names the real default. Tests cover each.

2026-11-09.
